Summary: Thoughts on bag o' holding bug
Keywords: loadstone, floatstone, holding


We should get rid of the bag-of-holding bug, but it's a neat idea to be
able to carry excess weight under certain circumstances.

Since we already have loadstones, why not hack 'floatstones' into the
game, that have negative weight?  If you had enough floatstones, you
could carry anything.

Just floatstones would be a very simple hack -- I suppose you might have
to watch out for strange possibilities like negative weight.  Perhaps
negative weight should cause levitation or perhaps paralysis in the
same way that excess weight does ("You are pinned against the ceiling")

Elaborations:
Perhaps one should only be able to pick up floatstones while levitating.
(But then how could one explain seeing them when looking at the floor?)
Perhaps floatstones should allow one to cross water safely (like vampires
do?)  (This would provide an answer to the people who complain about
drowning being too easy)
Perhaps #dipping a loadstone into a (blessed?) potion of levitation would 
make a floatstone.  This would be in keeping with Hack's spirit of having
nothing bad that can't be turned to ones advantage.  (Can't make floatstones 
from ordinary rocks; that would be too easy.)  Perhaps floatstones should be 
made by dipping stones of some sort into gain level potions.

